1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,380
You hear a song or a cold wind hits

2
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:05,060
you and suddenly every hair on your arms stands

3
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:06,920
straight up. You see,

4
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:09,560
each hair has a tiny muscle attached to it,

5
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:12,280
and when your brain feels a jolt of cold,

6
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:14,900
fear, or emotion, it squeezes all of them at

7
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:17,260
once, pulling your skin into bumps.

8
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:18,940
For our furry ancestors,

9
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:21,380
this fluffed up their fur to trap warm air

10
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:22,820
and make them look bigger,

11
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:24,580
just like a scared cat.

12
00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:26,520
But since we lost most of our fur,

13
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:28,160
it barely does anything for us.

14
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:31,300
And they're called goosebumps because your skin ends up

15
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:32,900
looking like a plucked goose.
